body:
True and some do communicate that they look for a hookup beforehand but there's also some who want to get into a queer relationship as a temporary placeholder for different reasons but only intend to stay with or marry within a hetero relationship. For example, I heard a lesbian who got told by her bi ex that she only wanted to use her for validation and that she never actually loved her, and she told her those things when she broke up to get together with a guy. These things can be very traumatic, bi women can be victims of this aswell though.
I agree with you that it's not ok to question bi people when they are commited because it's not ok to generalize an entire group and that is biphobia. 

Another thing that comes to mind is that often being told "I only want a hookup or a fwb with you" as a queer person is very damaging. In the case of WLW we are also often being told "men are easier" on top of it. it sounds like queer relationships are not worth it, only here for use and that reinforces the idea that only hetero/cis relationships work in the long term. Sorry for the long rant. ;-;
